// RULED (Eric, 2026-08-14): WHOLE-DERIVATION — a depth trip bottoms
// the entire function call at the root, with log::error at the trip
// (a program hitting the limit is a serious problem for the user).
// Implementation: ctx.depth_tripped is set at the trip and cleared
// when the derivation's root pops the depth to 0; while set, the
// select scrutinee ride refuses (no stale fragment may be assembled
// mid-unwind) and a tainted guard's held ride reads FALSE (the
// kernel's tainted-guard mask). The kernel needed only the log — its
// value-level trip propagation with no interior ride storage already
// implements the ruling. Both engines agree; the old interp behavior
// (per-level unwind with retained-instance rides, ambient-depth
// sensitive) is repealed.
//
// aug13j hz0 fuzz divergence_000000 (2026-08-13 night, seeds 4400M —
// LATENT, reproduces identically at ac432b6a pre-aug13i-fixes).
//
// THE FORK: what is the scope of a depth trip's bottom — the tripping
// DISPATCH (per-level unwind), or the whole DERIVATION?
//
// x=2's cycle: f(2) is value-infinite (every level re-calls f(x) via
// the capture) -> trip at depth 256 -> settled FreshBottom.
//
// INTERP (per-level unwind, = the written rulings composed): the trip
// bottoms level 256; each level above consumes its callee's bottom by
// the ordinary rules. Fresh interior instances (levels 2..255, minted
// this cycle) have no ride history -> stay bottom (aug04b phantom
// rule). But the ONE RETAINED instance — the outer body's second
// callsite B, which computed f(0)=0 on the x=0 cycle — has a cached
// scrutinee: the aug06 SCRUTINEE RIDE fires, B rides arm 1's 0 out
// stale, and the root emits n - 0 = 1 FIRED. Defensible: the
// hand-inlined chain of 256 distinct functions would unwind exactly
// this way (recursion-fires-like-chain).
//
// KERNEL (whole-derivation bottom): the native recursion's trip
// (graphix_depth_push fail) bottoms the ENTIRE invocation — no
// interior unwind, no rides — root quiet. Defensible: the depth
// limit is a budget on the DERIVATION the outermost call initiated;
// per-level unwind makes the observable VALUE depend on which
// interior level the global limit happened to fall at (ambient-depth
// sensitivity — the same f(2) called from depth 10 vs depth 250
// produces differently-shaped ride opportunities). Also structural:
// per-SITE ride storage cannot represent per-ACTIVATION rides (the
// parked interior-activation item), so the kernel cannot implement
// the interp's reading without per-activation value state.
//
// OPTIONS: (a) rule per-level -> kernel needs per-activation ride
// storage or must de-fuse recursive callees containing rideable
// selects (big coverage loss); (b) rule whole-derivation -> interp's
// trip return poisons the unwind chain (small change, only affects
// already-degraded logged-error programs, kills the ambient-depth
// sensitivity); (c) document as accepted divergence under depth trip
// (degraded mode). Recommend (b) on the straight-face test.
//
// interp: [1:-1 2:1] (rr_b minimal); jit: [1:-1]
{let x = array::iter([i64:0, i64:2]); let rec f = |n: i64| -> i64 select n {i64:0 => i64:0, _ => n - f(f(x))}; f(x - i64:1)}
